 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "Bundle rules are recorded at declaration time and replayed onto the app at registration.\n\n1. **Declaration:** `Bundle.attach_route_rule` (`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:413`), which `route`/`get`/`post` in `Scaffold` call (`src/tessel/sansio/scaffold.py:370`). It does not touch the app. It calls `Bundle.record(...)` (`bundles.py:224`) with a lambda that takes a `BundleSetupState` and appends it to `self.deferred_functions`.\n\n2. **Registration:** `App.register_bundle` (`src/tessel/sansio/app.py:571`) calls `bundle.register(app, options)` (`app.py:596`).\n\n3. **Replay:** `Bundle.register` (`bundles.py:273`) builds a `BundleSetupState` (`make_setup_state`, `bundles.py:253`). It then runs each `deferred_functions` entry with that state (`bundles.py:334`). It also registers any nested bundles (`bundles.py:377`).\n\n4. **Attaching to the app:** each lambda calls `BundleSetupState.attach_route_rule` (`bundles.py:87`). That method:\n   - joins `url_prefix` onto the rule;\n   - sets the subdomain and `url_defaults`;\n   - prefixes the endpoint as `<name_prefix>.<bundle name>.<endpoint>`;\n   - calls `self.app.attach_route_rule(...)`.\n\n5. **Final step:** `App.attach_route_rule` (`src/tessel/sansio/app.py:606`) adds the rule to `url_map` and stores the view in `view_functions`.",
